				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				14.60
			</span></i>: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγωνίᾱκα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερ-</span>) [<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				61.28
			</span></i>:—<i>contend eagerly, struggle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.61
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἀλλήλους</span> Isoc.l.c.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be distressed</i> or <i>anxious, be in an agony</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραχύνθαι τε καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					333e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγωνιῶντα καὶ τεθορυβημένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					210e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				869b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Her.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
